<title>MALAYSIA: Bescorp asks for stock suspension.</title>
<headline>Bescorp asks for stock suspension.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Construction and infrastructure firm Bescorp Industries Bhd said it was asking for trading suspension of its stock on Tuesday pending a news announcement.</p>
<p>The company did not give any other detail in its one-paragraph statement to the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Bescorp in January said it had signed an agreement with two Indian companies for a proposed joint venture to build a 300 megawatt thermal power plant in India.</p>
<p>The stock was last traded at 23.80 ringgit on Monday.</p>
</text>
